/gradlew text eol=lf
*.bat text eol=crlf
*.jar binary

# The generated API contract artifacts, compared BYTE FOR BYTE by
# ApiSurfaceSnapshotTest and by the browser's contract guard. Pinned to LF so
# that comparison means the same thing on Windows and on Linux.
#
# Scoped to these two filenames DELIBERATELY. A blanket `* text=auto eol=lf`
# renormalises the ENTIRE repository: every CRLF-checked-out file becomes
# modified at once, the next `git status` is unreadable, and the next commit is
# a whole-repo line-ending diff. It would also silently override the
# `*.bat text eol=crlf` rule above, which exists because .bat files need CRLF.
api-surface.txt text eol=lf
api-vocabulary.json text eol=lf
# The ACB run-window fixture: generated here, copied to the client, compared byte for byte.
debit-window.json text eol=lf
# The seed's debit-order population: generated by DebitOrderSeedGenerator and asserted byte for byte
# by the fast lane, so it is pinned by name like the artefacts above (F58).
src/main/resources/data/debit_order_members.json text eol=lf
# Month end's seed resources: generated by planning/branches/monthly-menu/legacy/reference.py --resource from SASBO's
# printed reports, and proved identical to what it generates by its --resource-check (01.1, 01.2, BR54).
src/main/resources/data/sasbo_reference_lists.json text eol=lf
src/main/resources/data/sasbo_workplaces.json text eol=lf
# SASBO's own history of branch visits: the months the branch list prints, by legacy/reference.py --resource (A.1).
src/main/resources/data/sasbo_workplace_visits.json text eol=lf
# The invented members who stand at them: generated by DemonstrationMemberGenerator and asserted byte for byte (01.4).
src/main/resources/data/demonstration_members.json text eol=lf
# Month end's rules, seeded: generated by MonthEndRulesSeedGenerator and asserted byte for byte (October build).
src/main/resources/data/month_end_rules_members.json text eol=lf
# The October demonstration population, every region's areas: generated by DemonstrationPopulationGenerator, byte for byte.
src/main/resources/data/demonstration_population.json text eol=lf
# The screens' answers over the seeded demonstration on 14 Oct 2026, for the presentation: generated by DemoAnswersTest.
src/test/resources/demo/demo-answers-2026-10-14.json text eol=lf
# Month end's golden answers: generated by MonthEndExamplesTest, copied to the client byte for byte (MD48, BR54).
month-end-examples.json text eol=lf
